{
  "profile": "strand",
  "profile_page": "profiles/strand.md",
  "notes": [
    "strand: strandOf(world, reader) answers {narrative, event, location, character, now, same}; the world carries its elements as the owner is served them, the ids its hidden mark keeps (hidden), and its readers, exactly as the lens and charter fixtures do. Each filled slot is {id, name}; an empty slot is null.",
    "readers: a reader's rung is owner (the whole world), contributor (the world less the hidden), guest (exactly the whole and known_of ids it lists; a known_of id is a stub: type and name, no links; hidden beats known_of) or public (the world less the hidden and the room elements). The strand reader resolves every slot through that one view and keeps no second copy of the rule.",
    "the key: the fixture gives x_strand as stored; the server's rule 1 (no key served when the named Narrative is out of the reader's view) is keel's test, not the reader's. A reader handed a key it cannot resolve answers an empty strand.",
    "mark: the value is an object with three string members, narrative, event and location; any other shape (a bare string, a missing member) reads as no mark: every slot null, same null. A reader needs no id-format test: an id that names no element in the view is an empty slot; the doctor names the shape.",
    "stub: a narrative the reader knows only as a stub fills the narrative slot ({id, name}) and nothing else, since a stub serves no events and no protagonist.",
    "order: the reading never depends on a multi-link's order; the event must be IN the narrative's events and the location IN the event's locations, position ignored.",
    "no fallback: character comes from protagonist only, never from the event's characters; location from the mark only, never from the character's location; now from the character's location only.",
    "same: true when now and location are both set and the same id; false when both set and different; null when either is null.",
    "kind: a slot holds only its own kind; an id of another kind in the mark or in a parent's list leaves the slot empty. same compares ids, never names."
  ],
